  "title": "2026-09-08-comp-134600 · agent-session-orchestration",
  "description": "# Long-lived agent session orchestration\nRead from admission at upper left into the runner's model/tool loop. The shared API authenticates and resolves workspace quotas; scheduling honors capacity, residency and isolation. The orchestrator builds requests from system context, history and permitted tools, appends results and advances turns.\n\nBlue paths represent durable output and checkpoints: live output reaches the client while identical output and audit events enter the event log. Reattachment replays after the last acknowledged position; disconnection does not cancel work. Each completed turn snapshots conversation, tools and files as content-addressed, parent-linked immutable state.\n\nThe orange lifecycle region covers suspension/interruption, heartbeat rescue, snapshot rehydration on an available host and continuation. Recovery replays at most the in-flight turn; externally mutating tools use idempotency keys. Interruption stops streams, attempts tool termination, records uncertain outcomes and checkpoints before release. Rolling deployments refuse new placements on old hosts and drain safely.\n\nThe lower-left tree expands concurrent child sessions and result return through the parent, with scoped context and parent-funded budgets. Its policy note covers workspace/tree quota aggregation, user-decision pauses, held-child accounting, cancellation/failure propagation and orphan reaping. The durability notes describe audit-driven metering and costs. The bottom inset shows original and forked futures sharing an earlier immutable snapshot; reachability determines collection eligibility.",
